## Local workflow

```bash
mise trust
mise install
mise run check
{% if stack == 'python' or stack == 'typescript' or stack == 'dotnet' or (stack == 'other' and run_tests) %}
mise run test
{% endif %}
```

`mise run check` runs `pre-commit run --all-files`, the same hook configuration CI uses. It installs the toolchains declared in `mise.toml` first.

{% if stack == 'python' %}
`mise run test` runs pytest and writes `coverage/coverage.xml`.
{% elif stack == 'typescript' %}
`mise run test` runs Vitest with coverage and writes `coverage/coverage-final.json` and `coverage/lcov.info`.
{% elif stack == 'dotnet' %}
`mise run test` runs `dotnet test` and writes Cobertura coverage under `coverage/`.
{% elif stack == 'other' and run_tests %}
`mise run test` runs the repository's native test task. This template never creates that task; add it to `mise.toml` before enabling CI tests.
{% elif stack == 'unity' %}
Unity integrity checks do not need the editor:

```bash
uvx --from git+https://github.com/{{ owner }}/dev-platform@{{ platform_ref }}#subdirectory=cli devctl unity integrity
```

{% if unity_runner == 'none' %}
No Unity runner is configured; CI calls `unity.yml` with `unity-runner: none` and runs integrity only. Unity tests and builds are skipped.
{% elif unity_runner == 'self-hosted' %}
Full Unity verification runs on the private repository's self-hosted runner (`unity-runner: self-hosted`), labelled `[self-hosted, windows, unity]`.
{% else %}
CI uses Unity Build Automation for a cloud build (`unity-runner: uba`); integrity still runs on GitHub-hosted runners. The cloud build is not a test check and never substitutes for the EditMode suite. Set the `UNITY_BUILD_API_KEY`, `UNITY_BUILD_ORG_ID` and `UNITY_BUILD_PROJECT_ID` secrets before the first run.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

## Continuous integration

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` calls the shared platform workflows at `{{ platform_ref }}`. It also runs on pull requests, so the required checks are the same for humans and automation.

{% if stack == 'unity' and unity_runner == 'none' %}
Required checks are `platform-verify / integrity` and `platform-security / scan`. No Unity test or build check is required because no Unity runner is configured.
{% elif stack == 'unity' and unity_runner == 'self-hosted' %}
Required checks are `platform-verify / integrity`, `platform-verify / tests` and `platform-security / scan`. Unity tests run only on a runner labeled `[self-hosted, windows, unity]`.
{% elif stack == 'unity' %}
Required checks are `platform-verify / integrity` and `platform-security / scan`. The `platform-verify / cloud-build` check appears only when Unity files change and is not a required check.
{% elif stack == 'other' %}
Required checks are `platform-verify / check`{% if run_tests %}, `platform-verify / test`{% endif %} and `platform-security / scan`.
{% else %}
Required checks are `platform-verify / check`, `platform-verify / test` and `platform-security / scan`.
{% endif %}

## Dependency updates

Renovate reads `renovate.json` and extends the shared preset `github>{{ owner }}/dev-platform`. It pins GitHub Actions to commit digests, groups template updates and automerges minor, patch and digest updates after the required checks pass.

